{"_id":"v4KxNp8TwQ3mRjA2","name":"Criminal","type":"class","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"description":"<p>Much of the Rim is far from the reach of anything resembling government oversight or corporate control. Criminal enterprises have found fertile ground to grow in these far reaches, and the desperate or unscrupulous flock to them.</p><h3>D10 Criminal Loadouts</h3><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>0</strong></td><td>Civilian Clothes (AP 1), Portable Computer Terminal, HUD, Satchel, Caffeine Pills</td></tr><tr><td><strong>1</strong></td><td>Civilian Clothes (AP 1), Bioscanner, Electronic Tool Set, Lockpick Set, Screwdriver</td></tr><tr><td><strong>2</strong></td><td>Standard Crew Attire (AP 1), Revolver (12 shots), Binoculars, Stun Baton</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3</strong></td><td>Heavy Duty Work Clothes (AP 2), Tranq Pistol (6 shots), Drill, Lockpick Set, Forged ID Badge</td></tr><tr><td><strong>4</strong></td><td>Vaccsuit (AP3), Laser Cutter (charged), Crowbar, Chemlight (x5)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>5</strong></td><td>Vaccsuit (AP3), SMG (2 shots), Mag Boots, Satchel, Recreational Drugs (12 doses)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>6</strong></td><td>Salvaged Armor (AP 4), Rigging Gun, Infrared Goggles, Electronic Tool Kit</td></tr><tr><td><strong>7</strong></td><td>Salvaged Armor (AP 4), Revolver (12 shots), Rucksack, Pain Pills</td></tr><tr><td><strong>8</strong></td><td>Corporate Attire (AP1), Compact Pistol (as Revolver but easily hidden, 6 shots), Recreational Drugs (2 doses)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>9</strong></td><td>Standard Battle Dress (AP 7), Combat Shotgun (12 shots), Stimpak (x5)</td></tr></tbody></table>","source":"","author":"","link":"","trauma_response":"When you make a Fear save you can make another close friendly player make it instead of you.","robotic":false,"common_skills":[],"base_adjustment":{"strength":0,"speed":0,"intellect":0,"combat":5,"sanity":0,"fear":0,"body":10,"max_wounds":0,"skills_granted":[]},"selected_adjustment":{"choose_stat":[{"modification":5,"stats":["strength","speed"]}],"choose_skill_and":{"trained":0,"expert":0,"expert_full_set":0,"master":0,"master_full_set":0},"choose_skill_or":[[{"name":"Computers (Trained)","trained":1,"expert":0,"expert_full_set":0,"master":0,"master_full_set":0,"from_list":[]},{"name":"Chemistry (Trained)","trained":1,"expert":0,"expert_full_set":0,"master":0,"master_full_set":0,"from_list":[]}],[{"name":"1 Expert Skill","trained":0,"expert":1,"expert_full_set":0,"master":0,"master_full_set":0,"from_list":[]},{"name":"2 Trained Skills","trained":2,"expert":0,"expert_full_set":0,"master":0,"master_full_set":0,"from_list":[]}]]},"roll_tables":{"loadout":"","trinket":"","patch":""}},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.13","coreVersion":"13.0","createdTime":1758506400000,"modifiedTime":1758506400000,"lastModifiedBy":""}}
{"_id":"w8JmKp5vNq1rXT6y","name":"Robot","type":"class","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"description":"<p>Out on the Rim, many old model mechanical automatons are still in service, the new human-like androids being too expensive or untrusted. Their toughness is testament to their original functions, but their old model logic cores are not sophisticated and they are far past their warranty expiration.</p><p><em>Robots don't need to breathe or wear vaccsuits.</em></p><h3>D10 Robot Loadouts</h3><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>0</strong></td><td>Mop and bucket, cleaning chemicals, hi-viz vest (AP 1), personal locator</td></tr><tr><td><strong>1</strong></td><td>Mag boots, short range comms, nail gun (32 shots), assorted toolkit</td></tr><tr><td><strong>2</strong></td><td>Hand welder, rigging gun (2 shots), radio jammer, explosives and detonator</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3</strong></td><td>SMG (10 shots), body cam, sunglasses, razor mohawk, brightly spray-painted body</td></tr><tr><td><strong>4</strong></td><td>Flamethrower (4 shots), bioscanner, rat poison (5 doses), gas mask (decorative)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>5</strong></td><td>Fire-resistant coating, foam gun (3 shots), short range comms, boarding axe</td></tr><tr><td><strong>6</strong></td><td>Mini-treads leg replacement, emergency beacon, flare gun (6 shots), sample collection kit</td></tr><tr><td><strong>7</strong></td><td>Cybernetic diagnostic scanner, electronic toolkit, portable computer terminal, revolver (12 shots)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>8</strong></td><td>Armored exoskeleton (AP 7), combat shotgun (4 shots), bioscanner, hit list</td></tr><tr><td><strong>9</strong></td><td>Extra arm, SMG x2 (20 shots), vibechete, self-destruct mechanism</td></tr></tbody></table>","source":"","author":"","link":"","trauma_response":"When you gain a Wound, also lose 1d10 from a stat or save.","robotic":true,"common_skills":[],"base_adjustment":{"strength":30,"speed":-10,"intellect":-10,"combat":0,"sanity":0,"fear":60,"body":0,"max_wounds":2,"skills_granted":[]},"selected_adjustment":{"choose_stat":[],"choose_skill_and":{"trained":0,"expert":0,"expert_full_set":0,"master":0,"master_full_set":0},"choose_skill_or":[[{"name":"1 Expert Skill","trained":0,"expert":1,"expert_full_set":0,"master":0,"master_full_set":0,"from_list":[]},{"name":"2 Trained Skills","trained":2,"expert":0,"expert_full_set":0,"master":0,"master_full_set":0,"from_list":[]}]]},"roll_tables":{"loadout":"","trinket":"","patch":""}},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.13","coreVersion":"13.0","createdTime":1758506400000,"modifiedTime":1758506400000,"lastModifiedBy":""}}
{"_id":"rN5gP2kT8mJ4vQx7","name":"Ranger","type":"class","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"description":"<p>Rangers are the ones they send to set foot on new worlds, answer distress calls, or otherwise be a first responder. Most rangers end up dying in horrible ways. The ones that survive tend to be tough enough to live through anything the universe throws at them.</p><h3>D10 Ranger Loadouts</h3><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>0</strong></td><td>Standard Crew Attire (AP 1), Combat Knife (1d10 DMG), Binoculars, Long Range Comms, Emergency Beacon</td></tr><tr><td><strong>1</strong></td><td>Heavy Duty Work Clothes (AP 2), Hand Welder, Crowbar, Bioscanner</td></tr><tr><td><strong>2</strong></td><td>Fatigues (AP 2), Vibechete, MoHab Unit, Water Filtration Device, Flashlight</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3</strong></td><td>Vaccsuit (AP 3), SMG (3 shots), HUD, Drone (recon)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>4</strong></td><td>Vaccsuit (AP 3), Tranq Gun (6 shots), Bioscanner, Medscanner, First Aid Kit, Pain Pills</td></tr><tr><td><strong>5</strong></td><td>Vaccsuit (AP 3), Rigging Gun, Hand Welder, Paracord, Patch Kit (x2)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>6</strong></td><td>Hazard Suit (AP 5), Revolver (12 shots), Bioscanner, Geiger Counter, Radiation Pills (x5)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>7</strong></td><td>Hazard Suit (AP 5), Combat Shotgun (8 shots), MoHab Unit, Combat Knife (as Scalpel), Water Filtration Device</td></tr><tr><td><strong>8</strong></td><td>Hazard Suit (AP 5), Foam Gun (3 shots), Boarding Axe, Folding Stretcher, First Aid Kit</td></tr><tr><td><strong>9</strong></td><td>Standard Battle Dress (AP 7), Pulse Rifle (3 shots), Body Cam, Flare Gun (2 shots)</td></tr></tbody></table>","source":"","author":"","link":"","trauma_response":"Once per session when you Panic, you can choose to take 2 stress instead.","robotic":false,"common_skills":[],"base_adjustment":{"strength":0,"speed":10,"intellect":5,"combat":0,"sanity":0,"fear":5,"body":5,"max_wounds":0,"skills_granted":[]},"selected_adjustment":{"choose_stat":[],"choose_skill_and":{"trained":2,"expert":0,"expert_full_set":0,"master":0,"master_full_set":0},"choose_skill_or":[]},"roll_tables":{"loadout":"","trinket":"","patch":""}},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.13","coreVersion":"13.0","createdTime":1758506400000,"modifiedTime":1758506400000,"lastModifiedBy":""}}
{"_id":"Rt4rY2kM7pN9vXj3","name":"Retiree","type":"class","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"description":"<p>Some people manage to survive all the way to retirement, but all that free time in a retirement facility wasn't all it cracked up to be. Sure, sometimes the crew rolls their eyes when you go on about how things worked in your day. They should really learn to respect their elders.</p><h3>D10 Retiree Loadouts</h3><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>0</strong></td><td>Hawai'ian Shirt and Shorts (AP 1), Fruity Cocktail Drink in Elaborate Container, Pain Pills</td></tr><tr><td><strong>1</strong></td><td>Tracksuit and Plastic Visor (AP 1), Revolver (6 shots), Deck of Cards, Coupons</td></tr><tr><td><strong>2</strong></td><td>Worn Work Clothes (AP 1), Wood Axe (as Boarding Axe), Woodworking Tools, Mylar Blanket</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3</strong></td><td>Worn Jumpsuit (AP 1), Wrench, Pocket Knife (as Scalpel), Flashlight, 6 Pack of Beer</td></tr><tr><td><strong>4</strong></td><td>Button Down Shirt and Slacks (AP 1), Electronics Tool Kit, Geiger Counter, Infrared Goggles, Short Range Comms</td></tr><tr><td><strong>5</strong></td><td>Civilian Clothes (AP 1), Camera, Paper System Map, Satchel</td></tr><tr><td><strong>6</strong></td><td>Nice Outfit (AP 1), Pet (Cat or Small Dog), Roller Suitcase, Oxygen Tank</td></tr><tr><td><strong>7</strong></td><td>Cozy Sweater and Corduroys (AP 1), Hunting Rifle (Range: Long, 2d10 DMG, 6 shots), Binoculars, Rucksack</td></tr><tr><td><strong>8</strong></td><td>Golf Sweater and Slacks (AP 1), Golf Clubs (as Crowbar), Medscanner, Bottle of Whiskey, Sense of Entitlement</td></tr><tr><td><strong>9</strong></td><td>Corporate Attire (AP 1), VIP Corporate Card (Retired), Personal Locator, An Obscene Amount of Credits and Refusal to Spend Them</td></tr></tbody></table>","source":"","author":"","link":"","trauma_response":"When you Panic make a Body save or suffer a heart attack (Unconscious, death in 1d10 rounds if not treated).","robotic":false,"common_skills":[],"base_adjustment":{"strength":0,"speed":-15,"intellect":0,"combat":0,"sanity":0,"fear":30,"body":-15,"max_wounds":0,"skills_granted":[]},"selected_adjustment":{"choose_stat":[{"modification":10,"stats":["strength","intellect","combat"]}],"choose_skill_and":{"trained":0,"expert":0,"expert_full_set":0,"master":0,"master_full_set":0},"choose_skill_or":[[{"name":"1 Master Skill (+ Expert & Trained Prerequisites)","trained":0,"expert":0,"expert_full_set":0,"master":0,"master_full_set":1,"from_list":[]},{"name":"2 Expert Skills (+ 2 Trained Prerequisites each)","trained":0,"expert":0,"expert_full_set":2,"master":0,"master_full_set":0,"from_list":[]}]]},"roll_tables":{"loadout":"","trinket":"","patch":""}},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.13","coreVersion":"13.0","createdTime":1758506400000,"modifiedTime":1758506400000,"lastModifiedBy":""}}
{"_id":"Py5cHiKpS2mNvT8r","name":"Psychic","type":"class","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"description":"<p>Certain rare people have been manifesting strange psychic powers. Rumors abound about hyperspace side effects and secret corporate experiments, but no one truly knows why this is happening. Psychics are often treated with suspicion and fear unless someone wants to take advantage of their abilities.</p><p><strong>Skills:</strong> Linguistics, Psychology</p><p><strong>Psionics:</strong> Psychics gain the Potential stat (roll 2d10+10 for starting score). Roll 1d100 under your Potential to use a psionic ability. On a success it works as planned and your Potential decreases by the amount rolled (fully recovered with rest). On a failure it works but you gain 1 Stress and all Potential drains until rest. A critical success works better than expected and increases your max Potential by 1d10. A critical failure goes catastrophically wrong and decreases your max Potential by 1d10. If your max Potential ever reaches zero, you lose all psychic capabilities forever.</p><p>Roll on the Psionic Abilities table a number of times equal to the tens digit of your Potential. A repeated roll levels up that ability instead. If your Potential\u2019s tens digit increases, roll a new ability or level up an existing one. You do not lose abilities even if your max Potential decreases.</p><h3>D10 Psychic Loadouts</h3><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>0</strong></td><td>Civilian Clothes (AP 1), Rucksack, Pet</td></tr><tr><td><strong>1</strong></td><td>Civilian Clothes (AP 1), Combat Knife (1d10 DMG), Lockpick Set, Recreational Drugs (2 doses), Criminal Contact</td></tr><tr><td><strong>2</strong></td><td>Standard Crew Attire (AP 1), Revolver (6 shots), Short Range Comms, First Aid Kit</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3</strong></td><td>Research Subject Jumpsuit (AP 1), Sample Kit, Medscanner, Personal Locator</td></tr><tr><td><strong>4</strong></td><td>Bloody Research Subject Jumpsuit (AP 1), Scalpel, Pain Pills, Personal Locator (damaged)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>5</strong></td><td>Vaccsuit (AP 3), Mag Boots, Patch Kit, Chemlight (x5)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>6</strong></td><td>Vaccsuit (AP 3), Nail Gun (32 shots), Crowbar</td></tr><tr><td><strong>7</strong></td><td>Experimental Psi Suit (AP 4, Increase range of psi effects one range until broken), Stimpak (x1), Body Cam, Personal Locator</td></tr><tr><td><strong>8</strong></td><td>Salvaged Armor (AP 4), Vibechete, Water Filtration Device, MRE (x7)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>9</strong></td><td>Standard Battle Dress (AP 7), Revolver (12 shots), Body Cam, Personal Locator</td></tr></tbody></table>","source":"","author":"","link":"","trauma_response":"While your Stress is 10 or higher, your Psionics rolls are at [\u2212].","robotic":false,"common_skills":[],"base_adjustment":{"strength":0,"speed":0,"intellect":20,"combat":0,"sanity":-10,"fear":30,"body":0,"max_wounds":0,"skills_granted":[]},"selected_adjustment":{"choose_stat":[],"choose_skill_and":{"trained":0,"expert":0,"expert_full_set":0,"master":0,"master_full_set":0},"choose_skill_or":[[{"name":"1 Expert Skill","trained":0,"expert":1,"expert_full_set":0,"master":0,"master_full_set":0,"from_list":[]},{"name":"2 Trained Skills","trained":2,"expert":0,"expert_full_set":0,"master":0,"master_full_set":0,"from_list":[]}]]},"roll_tables":{"loadout":"","trinket":"","patch":""}},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.13","coreVersion":"13.0","createdTime":1758679200000,"modifiedTime":1758679200000,"lastModifiedBy":""}}
{"_id":"Em8sYaRyKb3mVwQ6","name":"Emissary","type":"class","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"description":"<p>Somewhere at the edge of the known Rim you were reborn, rebuilt, or maybe created whole cloth, found only with a strange item. By what, you don't remember, but you're pretty sure they are watching through your eyes with cold curiosity. Human by all accounts. You have your doubts.</p><p><strong>Skills:</strong> Sophontology and Xenoesotericism (no prerequisite skills), 2 Trained skills, 1 Psionic ability (manifests as alien technology).</p><p><strong>Psionics:</strong> Emissaries gain a single psionic ability from the Psionic Abilities table. The ability manifests as alien technology rather than a natural talent, but functions identically. Emissaries also gain the Potential stat (roll 2d10+10).</p><h3>D10 Emissary Loadouts</h3><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>0</strong></td><td>Standard crew attire, part of your skin and can't be removed (DR 1).</td></tr><tr><td><strong>1</strong></td><td>Void glass knife. Can sever emotional bonds and excise memories.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>2</strong></td><td>Revolver, deals no DMG but causes the target to fall unconscious for 2d10 rounds. Fires 6 shots then never works again.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3</strong></td><td>Uniform with Company logo (the logo is wrong). Never gets dirty or torn (AP 1).</td></tr><tr><td><strong>4</strong></td><td>A radio, brightly colored like a children's toy. Signals aren't detected by normal comms. Receiving, you get messages from the recently deceased.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>5</strong></td><td>Vaccsuit (The oxygen tanks are filled with spongiform flesh. Always provides air if fed. AP 3).</td></tr><tr><td><strong>6</strong></td><td>Clothes of overlapping organic onionskin (AP 3). Regenerates AP after 54.6 hours.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>7</strong></td><td>Two metallic marbles suspended an inch apart. No amount of force can separate or compress them.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>8</strong></td><td>Full face insectoid helmet. Wearing it deprives all sensation.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>9</strong></td><td>Standard battle dress (AP 7). Autonomously moves and wraps you in a loving embrace at a command.</td></tr></tbody></table>","source":"","author":"","link":"","trauma_response":"You are unaffected by other player characters' trauma responses.","robotic":false,"common_skills":[],"base_adjustment":{"strength":0,"speed":0,"intellect":0,"combat":0,"sanity":30,"fear":30,"body":30,"max_wounds":0,"skills_granted":["Sophontology","Xenoesotericism"]},"selected_adjustment":{"choose_stat":[],"choose_skill_and":{"trained":2,"expert":0,"expert_full_set":0,"master":0,"master_full_set":0},"choose_skill_or":[]},"roll_tables":{"loadout":"","trinket":"","patch":""}},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null,"sort":0,"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.6.13","coreVersion":"13.0","createdTime":1758679200000,"modifiedTime":1758679200000,"lastModifiedBy":""}}
